  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe4;dda Barnen ECHO-Syria 2021-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xe4;dda Barnen ECHO-Syrien 2021-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe4;dda Barnen (Save the Children Sweden) has applied to Sida for funding of 2 527 500 SEK to carry out the EU-project &quot;Integrated child protection and education assistance responding to the most urgent needs of conflict-affected populations in North East and North West Syria&quot; during 2021-2022. 

The overall objective is: 

&#x201c;Providing needs-based education and child protection assistance to the most vulnerable children and their caregivers in North East and North West Syria&#x201d;.

The specific objective is:

&#x201c;Conflict affected boys and girls, and their families benefit from a strengthened child protection and education environment in North East and North West Syria&#x201d;.

The target population include adolescent girls and boys, children with disabilities (CwD), unaccompanied and separated children (UASC), children associated with armed forces and groups (CAAFAG), and others. 

The contribution has the EU Commission reference number ECHO/SYR/BUD/2021/91007. The contribution&apos;s total budget is 3 750 000 EUR, which corresponds to approximately 38 473 380 SEK. Of this, Save the Children has been granted 3 500 000 EUR fr&#xe5;n the European Commission and the requested support from Sida is 2 527 500  SEK, which corresponds to 7 % of the total budget.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xe4;dda Barnen har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering av egeninsats om 2&#xa0;527 500 SEK f&#xf6;r EU-projektet &quot;Integrated child protection and education assistance responding to the most urgent needs of conflict-affected populations in North East and North West Syria&quot; f&#xf6;r perioden 2021-2022.&#xa0;

Insatsens &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r:

&#x201c;Providing needs-based education and child protection assistance to the most vulnerable children and their caregivers in North East and North West Syria&#x201d;.

Insatsens specifika m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r:

&#x201c;Conflict affected boys and girls, and their families benefit from a strengthened child protection and education environment in North East and North West Syria&#x201d;.

Den prim&#xe4;ra m&#xe5;lgruppen &#xe4;r flickor och pojkar, barn med funktionsvariationer, ensamkommande flyktingbarn samt barn med kopplingar till v&#xe4;pnade styrkor och grupper. 

Den aktuella insatsen har EU-kommissionens referensnummer ECHO/SYR/BUD/2021/91007. Insatsen har en total budget p&#xe5; 3 750 000 EUR, vilket motsvarar cirka 38 473 380 SEK. Av detta har R&#xe4;dda Barnen beviljats 3 500 000 EUR fr&#xe5;n EU-kommissionen och ans&#xf6;ker om 2 527 500  SEK, cirka 7 %, fr&#xe5;n Sida.</narrative>
  </description>
